{"schema":1,"language":"en","set":{"id":"sma","name":"Hidden Fates Shiny Vault","releaseDate":"2019-08-23","cardCount":{"official":94,"total":94},"symbol":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/univ/sm/sma/symbol"},"cards":[{"id":"sma-SV1","localId":"SV1","name":"Scyther","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV1","description":"While young, they live together deep in the mountains, training themselves in how to fight with their scythes and move at high speeds."},{"id":"sma-SV10","localId":"SV10","name":"Quagsire","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV10","description":"This carefree Pokémon has an easygoing nature. While swimming, it always bumps into boat hulls."},{"id":"sma-SV11","localId":"SV11","name":"Froakie","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV11","description":"It protects its skin by covering its body in delicate bubbles. Beneath its happy-go-lucky air, it keeps a watchful eye on its surroundings."},{"id":"sma-SV12","localId":"SV12","name":"Frogadier","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV12","description":"Its swiftness is unparalleled. It can scale a tower of more than 2,000 feet in a minute's time."},{"id":"sma-SV13","localId":"SV13","name":"Voltorb","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV13","description":"Usually found in power plants. Easily mistaken for a Poké Ball, it has zapped many people."},{"id":"sma-SV14","localId":"SV14","name":"Xurkitree","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV14","description":"It appeared from the Ultra Wormhole. It raided a power plant, so people think it energizes itself with electricity."},{"id":"sma-SV15","localId":"SV15","name":"Seviper","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV15","description":"In battle, it uses its bladed tail to counter any Zangoose. It secretes a deadly venom in its tail."},{"id":"sma-SV16","localId":"SV16","name":"Shuppet","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV16","description":"It loves vengeful emotions and hangs in rows under the eaves of houses where vengeful people live."},{"id":"sma-SV17","localId":"SV17","name":"Inkay","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV17","description":"It flashes the light-emitting spots on its body, which drains its opponent's will to fight. It takes the opportunity to scuttle away and hide."},{"id":"sma-SV18","localId":"SV18","name":"Malamar","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV18","description":"It lures prey close with hypnotic motions, then wraps its tentacles around it before finishing it off with digestive fluids."},{"id":"sma-SV19","localId":"SV19","name":"Poipole","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV19","description":"This Ultra Beast is well enough liked to be chosen as a first partner in its own world."},{"id":"sma-SV2","localId":"SV2","name":"Rowlet","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV2","description":"This wary Pokémon uses photosynthesis to store up energy during the day, while becoming active at night."},{"id":"sma-SV20","localId":"SV20","name":"Sudowoodo","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV20","description":"To avoid attack, it mimics a tree. It will run off if splashed with water, which it hates."},{"id":"sma-SV21","localId":"SV21","name":"Riolu","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV21","description":"It's tough enough to run right through the night, and it's also a hard worker, but it's still just a youngster."},{"id":"sma-SV22","localId":"SV22","name":"Lucario","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV22","description":"They can detect the species of a living being—and its emotions—from over half a mile away. They control auras and hunt their prey in packs."},{"id":"sma-SV23","localId":"SV23","name":"Rockruff","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV23","description":"This Pokémon has lived with people since times long ago. It can sense when its Trainer is in the dumps and will stick close by its Trainer's side."},{"id":"sma-SV24","localId":"SV24","name":"Buzzwole","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV24","description":"A mysterious life-form called an Ultra Beast. Witnesses saw it pulverize a dump truck with a single punch."},{"id":"sma-SV25","localId":"SV25","name":"Zorua","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV25","description":"It changes so it looks like its foe, tricks it, and then uses that opportunity to flee."},{"id":"sma-SV26","localId":"SV26","name":"Guzzlord","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV26","description":"A dangerous Ultra Beast, it appears to be eating constantly, but for some reason its droppings have never been found."},{"id":"sma-SV27","localId":"SV27","name":"Magnemite","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV27","description":"It sends out electromagnetic waves, which let it float through the air. Touching it while it's eating electricity will give you a full-body shock."},{"id":"sma-SV28","localId":"SV28","name":"Magneton","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV28","description":"It has about three times the electrical power of Magnemite. For some reason, outbreaks of this Pokémon happen when lots of sunspots appear."},{"id":"sma-SV29","localId":"SV29","name":"Magnezone","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV29","description":"As it zooms through the sky, this Pokémon seems to be receiving signals of unknown origin, while transmitting signals of unknown purpose."},{"id":"sma-SV3","localId":"SV3","name":"Dartrix","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV3","description":"A bit of a dandy, it spends its free time preening its wings. Its preoccupation with any dirt on its plumage can leave it unable to battle."},{"id":"sma-SV30","localId":"SV30","name":"Beldum","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV30","description":"Its cells are all magnets. It uses magnetism to communicate with others of its kind."},{"id":"sma-SV31","localId":"SV31","name":"Metang","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV31","description":"When two Beldum link together, their psychic power is doubled. Their intelligence, however, remains unchanged."},{"id":"sma-SV32","localId":"SV32","name":"Celesteela","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV32","description":"One kind of Ultra Beast. Witnesses have seen it burn down a forest by expelling gas from its two arms."},{"id":"sma-SV33","localId":"SV33","name":"Kartana","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV33","description":"One of the Ultra Beast life-forms, it was observed cutting down a gigantic steel tower with one stroke of its blade."},{"id":"sma-SV34","localId":"SV34","name":"Ralts","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV34","description":"If its horns capture the warm feelings of people or Pokémon, its body warms up slightly."},{"id":"sma-SV35","localId":"SV35","name":"Kirlia","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV35","description":"The cheerful spirit of its Trainer gives it energy for its psychokinetic power. It spins and dances when happy."},{"id":"sma-SV36","localId":"SV36","name":"Diancie","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV36","description":"A sudden transformation of Carbink, its pink, glimmering body is said to be the loveliest sight in the whole world."},{"id":"sma-SV37","localId":"SV37","name":"Altaria","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV37","description":"On sunny days, it flies freely through the sky and blends into the clouds. It sings in a beautiful soprano."},{"id":"sma-SV38","localId":"SV38","name":"Gible","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV38","description":"It skulks in caves, and when prey or an enemy passes by, it leaps out and chomps them. The force of its attack sometimes chips its teeth."},{"id":"sma-SV39","localId":"SV39","name":"Gabite","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV39","description":"Shiny objects are its passion. It can be found in its cave, scarcely moving, its gaze fixed on the jewels it's amassed or Carbink it has caught."},{"id":"sma-SV4","localId":"SV4","name":"Wimpod","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV4","description":"This Pokémon is a coward. As it desperately dashes off, the flailing of its many legs leaves a sparkling clean path in its wake."},{"id":"sma-SV40","localId":"SV40","name":"Garchomp","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV40","description":"The protuberances on its head serve as sensors. It can even detect distant prey."},{"id":"sma-SV41","localId":"SV41","name":"Eevee","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV41","description":"Current studies show it can evolve into an incredible eight different species of Pokémon."},{"id":"sma-SV42","localId":"SV42","name":"Swablu","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV42","description":"It constantly grooms its cotton-like wings. It takes a shower to clean itself if it becomes dirty."},{"id":"sma-SV43","localId":"SV43","name":"Noibat","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV43","description":"They live in pitch black caves. Their enormous ears can emit ultrasonic waves of 200,000 hertz."},{"id":"sma-SV44","localId":"SV44","name":"Oranguru","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV44","description":"Deep in the jungle, high in the lofty canopy, this Pokémon abides. On rare occasions, it shows up at the beach to match wits with Slowking."},{"id":"sma-SV45","localId":"SV45","name":"Type: Null","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV45","description":"The heavy control mask it wears suppresses its intrinsic capabilities. This Pokémon has some hidden special power."},{"id":"sma-SV46","localId":"SV46","name":"Leafeon-GX","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV46"},{"id":"sma-SV47","localId":"SV47","name":"Decidueye-GX","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV47"},{"id":"sma-SV48","localId":"SV48","name":"Golisopod-GX","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/en/sm/sma/SV48"},{"id":"sma-SV49","localId":"SV49","name":"Charizard-GX","variants":{"normal":true,"holo":false,"reverse":false,"firstEdition":false,"wPromo":false},"image":"https://assets.tcgdex.net/